  "note": "PR (STV), polled 15 January 1920. South-East Area, three seats: 963 on the register, 410 valid, 31 spoilt. After Burke's surplus Wilson (102) and Anderson (98) were declared elected, \"there being no further surplus votes for distribution\"; John Mahaffy, who also stood in the North Area, was not elected here. Council after the election: 8 Labour, 5 Unionists, 1 Independent Labour, 1 Nationalist."
